  "body": {
    "id": "prop:dickman-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "In the homogeneous-residual special case \\(\\bar q(u)\\equiv c\\) and \\(r(u)\\equiv r(0)\\), the raw jump sum underlying \\(Z_{r,\\bar q}\\), after the declared centering and scaling, is the generalized Dickman law with parameter \\(c\\) studied by BhattacharjeeGoldstein2019. If \\(r(0)=0\\), then \\(Z_{r,\\bar q}=0\\) and the finite-transfer inequality specializes to \\(\\Pr(G_n^c\\cup\\{|\\widehat\\tau_n-\\tau_n|>4h_n\\})\\le D_{\\mathrm{tr},n}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "q",
      "c",
      "r",
      "Z",
      "tauhat",
      "tau",
      "n",
      "G",
      "h",
      "Dtransfer"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:intensity-class",
      "def:residual-class",
      "thm:finite-transfer",
      "lem:generalized-dickman-poisson-law"
    ],
    "justification": "The reduction checks that the new profile law agrees with a known limit under homogeneous residuals rather than renaming the Dickman distribution.",
    "gap": "BhattacharjeeGoldstein2019 settles the homogeneous weighted-sum limit; the present novelty begins with signed heterogeneous profiles, adaptive transfer, and inference.",
    "consumer": "Readers can validate the calibration code against a known one-parameter law before using general profiles.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(r_0=r(0)\\).  Under \\(\\bar q(u)\\equiv c\\) and\n\\(r(u)\\equiv r_0\\), define\n\\[\n J_c=\\int_{(0,1]}u\\,N_c(du),\\qquad\n N_c(du)\\ \\hbox{of intensity }c\\,du/u.\n\\]\nThe cited generalized-Dickman characterization identifies \\(J_c\\) with the generalized Dickman law of parameter \\(c\\).  Direct substitution in the definition of \\(Z\\) gives\n\\[\n Z_{r,\\bar q}\n =\\frac{r_0}{c}\\left\\{\\int_{(0,1]}u\\,N_c(du)\n       -\\int_0^1u\\,c\\,\\frac{du}{u}\\right\\}\n =\\frac{r_0}{c}(J_c-c).\n\\]\nThis is precisely the declared centering and scaling of the raw generalized-Dickman jump sum.  If \\(r_0=0\\), the homogeneous profile is identically zero, so the last display gives \\(Z_{r,\\bar q}=0\\).  Substitution into\n\\(\\mathrm{thm:finite\\mbox{-}transfer}\\), together with\n\\(S_n=\\widehat\\tau_n-\\tau_n\\), yields\n\\[\n \\Pr\\!\\left(G_n^c\\cup\n \\{|\\widehat\\tau_n-\\tau_n|>4h_n\\}\\right)\n \\leq D_{\\mathrm{tr},n}.\n\\]",
